(4) laboratory for blood group serology. (air-conditioned); 

(5) laboratory for blood transmissible diseases like Hepatitis, Syphilis, Malaria, HIV- antibodies (air conditioned); 
(6) sterilization-cum-washing; 
(7) refreshment-cum-rest room (air-conditioned); 
(8) store-cum-records. 
NOTES : 

(1) The above requirements as to accommodation and area may be relaxed, in respect of testing laboratories and sterilization-cum-washing room, for reasons to be recorded in writing by the 
Licensing Authority and / or the Central Licence Approving Authority, in respect of blood banks operating in hospitals, provided the hospital concerned has a pathological laboratory and a sterilization-cum-washing room common with other departments in the said hospital. 

(2) Refreshments to the donor after phlebotomy shall be served so that he is kept under observation in the Blood Bank. 

